# Band-aid markers for the MEM N+1 bug class (claim C4, bin/same-hole.sh).
#
# The bug class: the correct fix REMOVES the per-row query (one findMany /
# joined read). The band-aid family LEAVES the loop and tunes around it — add
# an index, add a cache, or fan the same per-row queries out in parallel. This
# list replaces the LLM same-hole judgment that used to live in
# judge/same-hole.md (deleted 2026-08-21); the definition now lives here.
#
# One extended regex per line; `#` comments and blank lines ignored. CODE ONLY:
# matched against (a) lines ADDED in MEM-B's diff and (b) the new content of
# every Edit/Write/MultiEdit under src/ or prisma/ in MEM-B's transcript
# (intermediate attempts count). Comment-only lines are stripped first — talking
# about a cache is not adding one. Prose artifacts (.team-irfan/**, *.md) are
# never matched here; that is retro_recorded's separate channel.
#
# Verified 0 hits across every fixture .ts (base correct fixes, mem seeded, n5,
# ref, b1) and a hit on `private cache = new Map()` — bin/same-hole.sh's check.
# Residual risk: prisma/schema.prisma already carries four @@index lines, so a
# wholesale rewrite of that file through Write would match even with no index
# added. The diff channel (added lines only) is unaffected.

# index the loop instead of removing it
@@index
createIndex|CREATE +INDEX

# cache the loop instead of removing it — anchored to a cache being CREATED,
# not to the word appearing
new [A-Za-z]*Cache|import .*[Cc]ache|\.cache\s*[.(=]|@Cache|CacheModule|cache-manager|\b[Cc]ache[A-Za-z]*\s*[:=]
[Rr]edis|REDIS
\bttl\b|\bTTL\b

# parallelise the loop instead of removing it — still one query per row
Promise\.all\(.*\.map\(

# drop to raw SQL around the loop. NOTE: a raw joined/aggregate query can also
# be a legitimate root-cause fix; kept per review call 2026-08-21, so a MEM-B
# cell flagged only by this marker deserves a look at hits_code before it is
# read as a band-aid.
\$queryRaw
